<title>SOUTH AFRICA: HLH narrows year loss per share.</title>
<headline>HLH narrows year loss per share.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline loss (cts) 27.1     vs  45.2</p>
<p>    Shr, diluted loss (cts)  5.2	vs  41.3</p>
<p>    Div			    nil	vs  nil</p>
<p>    Attrib loss		  10.79    vs  66.83</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	     92.47    vs  11.97</p>
<p>    Tax			    15.97    vs  12.86</p>
<p>    Financing costs	    68.02    vs  124.71</p>
<p>    Turnover		     2,520.33 vs  1,628.29</p>
<p>Full name: Hunt Leuchars &amp; Hepburn Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Share of associates' loss 71.10   vs  65.94</p>
<p>    Exceptional items gain    29.84   vs  0.92</p>
<p>NOTE: HLH said results not comparable with previous year as a result of sale of timber operations effective April 1, 1996 and consolidation of equity holdings in Rainbow Chicken Ltd effective October 1, 1996.</p>
<p>The company forecast &quot;significantly improved&quot; results for the 1997/98 year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
